\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In a related development announced on June 10, 2026, OpenView introduced its Luminous Virtual Windows, a solution described as transforming enclosed interiors into immersive environments filled with light, depth, and the sensation of open space. The product, which was awarded the 2025 Good Design Award from The Chicago Athenaeum: Museum of Architecture and Design and the European Centre for Architecture, Art, Design, and Urban Studies, employs advanced photographic techniques including focus stacking to generate a realistic sense of depth. Unlike traditional wall murals or standard panoramic photography, the system mimics the human eye's natural perception of depth by combining multiple images taken at different focus points into a single composite photograph. OpenView utilizes professional ultra-high-definition eight-channel printers to produce prints mounted onto optical-quality acrylic panels, with calibrated LED light boxes emitting a soft, natural luminescence that replicates daylight. The modular panels, reaching sizes of 5 by 8 feet, can be combined into larger window arrays and are designed to support long-term maintenance through easily replaceable LED components.}
