\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Turning to General Catalyst, the firm completed a significant take-private transaction on June 30, 2026, as Janus Henderson Group Ltd. finalized its transition to private ownership alongside Trian Fund Management and Qatar Investment Authority. Public shares were converted into cash at $52.00 per share and delisted from the New York Stock Exchange. Ali Dibadj, continuing as Chief Executive Officer, expressed enthusiasm about the new chapter, highlighting transformative opportunities in partnership with Trian and General Catalyst. Hemant Taneja, CEO of General Catalyst, remarked on the collaboration and stated the firm's commitment to enhancing Janus Henderson's technological capabilities and overall growth strategy. The transaction was supported by additional investors including MassMutual and Sun Hung Kai & Co., with the firm maintaining operational bases in London and Denver.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 General Catalyst also participated in a $1.5 million seed funding round for Gurugram-based Omli, announced on June 17, 2026. The round was led by India Quotient, with General Catalyst among the participating investors. Founded in 2025 by Shivam Munshi and Siddhant Garg, Omli develops AI infrastructure for children's speech and language development, addressing a gap in existing commercial speech recognition systems that are predominantly trained on adult voices. The company's flagship application, OmliKids, enables children aged three to ten years to engage in voice-based conversations with an AI companion named Doro, and has already achieved over 500,000 downloads on the Google Play Store within a few months of its launch. Omli has developed VedAnsh-v1, a proprietary speech-to-text and voice activity detection system, which has demonstrated significant improvements in word error rates compared to existing commercial systems. Co-founder Siddhant Garg emphasized the company's ambition to achieve adult-grade accuracy in children's speech recognition, including support for Indian accents and vernacular languages. India Quotient's Madhukar noted that children represent the largest consumer segment for which AI solutions are yet to be developed.}
