\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Also backed by Battery Ventures, Baz introduced Baz Planner at AI Engineer World's Fair on June 29, 2026, alongside the completion of an extended seed funding round raising an additional $9 million, bringing total funding to $17 million. The round was co-led by Battery Ventures and boldstart ventures, with participation from AFG Partners and Disruptive VC. Baz Planner is a gateway that sits between developers and the codebase, automatically routing ideas through dynamic loops that detect, root-cause, patch, and validate vulnerabilities and bugs. Guy Eisenkot, co-founder and CEO of Baz, stated, "Our clients have pushed us to intervene at the planning stage, where vulnerabilities and bugs are the cheapest to eliminate," adding that "Baz exists because they refuse to accept that AI-generated code means blindly accepting risk." Engineering teams using Baz Planner have reported up to a 65% reduction in downstream rework. Barak Schoster, Partner at Battery Ventures, described Baz as becoming "the super harness that coordinates coding agents to ensure AI-generated code ships safely and at scale." Baz has attracted over 100 leading AI, infrastructure, and cybersecurity customers globally, with its AI Code Review product ranked number one in precision-weighted Code Review Bench.}
